.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx-regen 1  "ngx-regen " 
.SH NAME
ngx\-regen \- Rewrite ngx\-managed sites with the current template (after an upgrade): diffs, one confirmation, one nginx \-t
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\-regen\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fISITES\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rewrite ngx\-managed sites with the current template (after an upgrade): diffs, one confirmation, one nginx \-t
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Every site created by ngx
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show the diffs without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fISITES\fR]
Site IDs or domains
.SH EXTRA
Your settings and snippets are kept; only the generated parts change.

Examples:
  sudo ngx regen \-\-all \-\-dry\-run
  sudo ngx regen \-\-all
  sudo ngx regen 3 4
